<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Savoie</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Savoie is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, with its prefecture at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chambery">Chambéry</a>, the old capital of the counts of Savoy. Together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haute-savoie">Haute-Savoie</a> it was formed from the historic Duchy of Savoy, which the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> ceded to France by the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a> in 1860 in return for French support for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-unification">Italian unification</a>. It belongs to the Auvergne-Rhône-Alpes region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/savoie.jpg" alt="Savoie" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas Eichler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2017.01.21.-02-Paradiski-La_Plagne-Dos_Rond--Blick_Richtung_Les_Arcs.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
